For~(ii), let $S$ be a set of $2k-1$ vertices of $\overline{H}_{2k}$. It is only possible that $S$ is included in an edge of $H$ if $S\cap A$ is an edge of $H$ and $|S \cap B| = k-1$, or the same with the roles of $A$ and $B$ reversed; without loss of generality we assume the former. A necessary condition for $\{x\} \cup S$ to be an edge of $\overline{H}_{2k}$ is then that $x\in B$ and that $\vphi_B(\{x\} \cup (S\cap B)) \in E(H)$. The number of such vertices $x$ is at most $d_H(\vphi_B(S\cap B)) \leq \Delta(H)$, so $d_{\overline{H}_{2k}}(S) \leq \Delta(H)$.
